  "kanji": "連",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 連\ntitle: link; take along\njlpt: 3\ntags: [jlpt-n3, grade-4, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 10\nradical: 辵\nradicalNumber: 162\nonyomi: [レン]\nkunyomi: [つら.なる, つら.ねる, つ.れる, -づ.れ]\ndistractors: [速, 週, 遠]\n---\n\n# 連 — link; take along\n\n**Strokes:** 10 · **Key (radical):** 辵 (as 辶, no. 162) · **JLPT:** N3 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n連 brings things or people together in a connected sequence. In [連休](../words/連休.md) れんきゅう, the days off follow one another;\nin 連れる つれる, someone takes another person along.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** use the visible 車 inside 辶 to imagine a line of vehicles travelling together.\nThe connected line is a mnemonic, not an etymology.\n\n## Readings\n\nThe table selects useful readings; the metadata preserves the complete source reading list.\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| レン | on | [連休](../words/連休.md) れんきゅう — consecutive days off; 連続 れんぞく — succession |\n| つ.れる | kun | 連れる つれる — take someone along |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [連休](../words/連休.md) れんきゅう — consecutive days off\n- 連れる つれる — take someone along\n- 連続 れんぞく — continuation; succession\n\n## Notes\n\n連れる is used with the person taken along: 子どもを連れる (こどもをつれる), \"take a child along.\"\nIts て-form is 連れて (つれて).\n[速](速.md) replaces the 車-shaped center with 束; the outer outline alone does not identify the character.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project).\nDictionary: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1559290, 1559380, 1559610.\n",
